23) diff between on and using 
Key Differences
• Column Names:
	• ON: Works even when the joined columns have different names (e.g., ON table1.id = table2.user_id).
	• USING: Requires the column names to be identical in both tables (e.g., USING (id)).
• Result Set Columns:
	• ON: Preserves both copies of the join columns separately in the output.
	• USING: Merges/coalesces the matching join columns into a single shared column in the final result.
• Condition Flexibility:
	• ON: Supports complex expressions, inequalities (<, >, !=), and multiple logical conditions.
	• USING: Tests strictly for equality (=) between the specified columns.
• Compatibility:
	• ON: Supported universally across all major SQL databases.
	• USING: Supported by MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, and BigQuery, but not by SQL Server (T-SQL)
 

